<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Crnojević</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1490">1490</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Crnojević was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a>, the forerunner of Montenegro, from 1465 to 1490. Caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, he fought the Ottomans in alliance with Venice and lost his lands for a time. In 1482 he moved his seat from Žabljak to the mountain stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje">Cetinje</a>, where he founded a monastery in 1484. His son Đurađ set up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press that produced the Oktoih in 1494.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-crnojevic.jpg" alt="Ivan Crnojević" width="219" height="334" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vittore Carpaccio Workshop · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Miracle_of_St._Tryphon,_ca._1506,_tempera_with_oil_paint_on_softwood_panel,_113_x_263_cm_(Ivan_Crnojevic).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
